    logP = 2.5);
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Budesonide is a corticosteroid used for inflammatory conditions such as asthma, Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis, and microscopic colitis. It is widely used and authorised in the European Union, where products cover areas such as IgA glomerulonephritis and esophageal diseases.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422212&quot;>Wikidata Q422212</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>budesonide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A07EA06, D07AC09, R01AD05, R03BA02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01222&quot;>DB01222</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5281004&quot;>5281004</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:3207&quot;>3207</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422212&quot;>Q422212</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C25H34O6</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>430.541 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
